        <mxCell id="e34" value="" style="endArrow=block;endFill=1;html=1;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#555555;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p3" target="p4"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e45" value="" style="endArrow=block;endFill=1;html=1;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#555555;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p4" target="p5"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e56" value="" style="endArrow=block;endFill=1;html=1;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#555555;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p5" target="p6"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="e67" value="" style="endArrow=block;endFill=1;html=1;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#555555;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;entryX=1;entryY=0.5;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p6" target="p7"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="eback" value="Next Sprint Cycle" style="endArrow=block;endFill=1;html=1;strokeWidth=2;strokeColor=#DC2626;fontStyle=1;fontSize=10;fontColor=#DC2626;exitX=0.5;exitY=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=1;curved=1;" edge="1" parent="1" source="p7" target="p2"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="why" value="WHY AGILE / SCRUM WAS CHOSEN FOR MitigatePlus" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fillColor=#F0FDF4;strokeColor=#16A34A;strokeWidth=1.5;fontSize=10;fontColor=#0D1B2A;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="100" y="620" width="880" height="210" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="whyd" value="1. Evolving Requirements: LGU disaster response protocols changed iteratively during stakeholder consultations with barangay officials.
2. Early Risk Detection: 2-week sprints exposed critical issues early (e.g., QR anti-duplicate race condition, localStorage vs AsyncStorage bug on mobile).
3. Continuous Deployment: GitHub → Vercel (web admin) and Render (backend) automated after each sprint review.
4. Stakeholder Validation: Sprint reviews with LGU officials ensured every feature matched real disaster response workflows before final deployment.
5. Working Software: Agile delivers tested, deployable increments each sprint — essential for capstone demonstration readiness." style="text;html=0;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=9;fontColor=#374151;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="108" y="652" width="864" height="172" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="roles" value="SCRUM TEAM COMPOSITION" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fillColor=#EFF6FF;strokeColor=#2563EB;strokeWidth=1.5;fontSize=10;fontColor=#0D1B2A;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1030" y="620" width="570" height="210" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="rolesd" value="Product Owner:
Represents LGU / DSWD stakeholder needs. Prioritizes and maintains the product backlog.

Scrum Master:
Facilitates sprint ceremonies, removes blockers, enforces Agile discipline.

Development Team:
Full-stack developers responsible for design, coding, testing, and deploying each feature increment across Web Admin, Backend, and Mobile platforms." style="text;html=0;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=9;fontColor=#374151;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1038" y="652" width="554" height="172" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
